{
  "requirement": "The `habeas-evidence` skill MUST tell agents not to write placeholder evidence for a requirement or example whose implementation is pending.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The requirement has one obligation: the `habeas-evidence` skill must tell agents not to write placeholder evidence when a requirement's or example's implementation is pending.\n\n`tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[the_evidence_skill_never_writes_placeholder_evidence_for_pending_work]` covers it. The test is marked `{test}`.\n\n- It reads the bundled `habeas-evidence` skill's Workflow section. The helpers `workflow_steps`, `step_of` and `step` parse the numbered steps. The test finds the step containing \"Stop and report each finding that needs the user\".\n- It then calls `assert_text_in_order` on that step's text. The call requires \"names only implementation that is still pending\" and, after it, \"never write placeholder evidence\". The helper panics if either phrase is missing or out of order.\n- The skill text in `assets/skills/habeas-evidence/SKILL.md` has the sentence this targets. The findings that need the user include \"a missing record or false judgment whose rationale names only implementation that is still pending, which is expected. Don't keep iterating on those, and never write placeholder evidence.\"\n\nThe assertion ties the prohibition to the pending-implementation case. It also fails if the prohibition is dropped, reworded, or moved to an unrelated step. The requirement states no other conditions, modes or boundaries, so no further scenarios are needed. There are no acknowledgments and no gaps.",
